(Studio: Russ Mitchell)  Report introduced.  {Ed: previous report aired until 5:20:50.}  

(Manchester, New Hampshire: Bianca Solarzano)  A look at the young swing voters in the swing state of New Hampshire presented; scenes shown of presidential candidates Senators Barack Obama and John McCain campaigning.  [New Hampshire Inst. of Politics Jennifer DONAHUE&#134;- says young people tend to vote left of center: that's Obama.]  [St. Anselm's College young voters Shay KELLY&#134;, Sam INMAN&#134;, Lauren CHOOLIJIAN&#134;- offer their views on the two candidates and the economy.]  Circle statistics on the voter turnout in 2004 and 2000 cited.  [McCain supporter Chris SMIGLOWSKI&#134;, Obama supporter Craig LeDUC&#134;- comment on the issues of taxes and the war.]  

(Studio: Russ Mitchell)  Technical problems acknowledged.
